  "title": "Instructions for the Fundi",
  "category": "home",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "level": 7,
  "order": 703,
  "theme": "home",
  "culturalNote": "In Kenya you don't call \"a plumber\" or \"an electrician\" — you call a fundi: fundi wa maji (plumber), fundi wa stima (electrician), fundi wa mbao (carpenter). Agreeing on the price before work starts is essential (\"tuongee bei kwanza\"). Giving instructions politely uses the subjunctive: \"urekebishe\" (please fix), \"usiguse\" (don't touch), \"uniambie\" (tell me). The everyday Kenyan word for electricity is stima; Sanifu prefers umeme.",
  "startingPoint": "Water is dripping from the bathroom ceiling. A fundi arrives at your flat.",
  "grammarFocus": [
    "subjunctive",
    "polite-requests",
    "perfect-me",
    "object-infixes"
  ],
